<newsitem itemid="232018" id="root" date="1996-12-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Finlay Enterprises Inc Q3 loss shrinks.</title>
<headline>Finlay Enterprises Inc Q3 loss shrinks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except share and per share data)</p>
<p>					   Thirteen Weeks Ended</p>
<p>				     November 2,     October 28,</p>
<p>					  1996		1995</p>
<p>    Sales			   $136,140	  $132,058</p>
<p>    EBITDA			  $7,105	    $5,782</p>
<p>    Net income (loss)	   $(2,637)	  $(2,760)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)/share applicable</p>
<p>    to common shares	    $(0.35)	   $(0.37)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding</p>
<p>					7,481,375	 7,456,885</p>
<p>					Thirty-Nine Weeks Ended</p>
<p>					November 2,     October 28,</p>
<p>					1996		1995</p>
<p>    Sales			   $404,047	  $380,202</p>
<p>    EBITDA			  $18,960	   $14,480</p>
<p>    Net income (loss)	   $(8,604)	  $(4,970)</p>
<p>Pro Forma(A):</p>
<p>    Net income (loss)	   $(8,604)	  $(9,496)</p>
<p>Net income (loss)/share applicable  </p>
<p>     to common shares	   $(1.15)	   $(1.28)</p>
<p>Weighted average shares outstanding</p>
<p>					7,481,182	 7,444,235</p>
<p>NOTE: (A) Pro forma amounts exclude the effect of the proceeds from life insurance totaling $5.0 million in the second quarter ended July 29, 1995, the company said.</p>
<p>Pro forma amounts assume the public offering and the related transactions including the $6.1 million Debenture repurchase, the Series C exchange, which resulted in a non-cash charge of $10 million and the interest rate reduction of 1/2 of 1 percent on the Revolving Credit Facility occurred immediately prior to the beginning of the 1995 fiscal year.</p>
<p>Excluding these pro forma adjustments, net loss applicable to common shares was $15,687,000 for the nine months ended October 28, 1995 and the net loss per share applicable to common shares for the nine months ended October 28, 1995 was $2.53, the company said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
